NAME
       vgchange - change a volume group, such as turning its volumes on or off

SYNOPSIS
       vgchange -a y|n [VG...]

DESCRIPTION
       vgchange changes the attributes of volume groups. Its everyday use is
       activation: an active logical volume has a device file
       (/dev/VG/LV) and can be used; an inactive one cannot. Volume groups
       are normally activated at boot by themselves.

OPTIONS
       -a, --activate y|n
              Activate (y) or deactivate (n) all logical volumes of the
              volume group. Unmount their file systems before deactivating.

EXAMPLES
           umount /mnt/data
           vgchange -a n vgdata
           vgchange -a y vgdata

SEE ALSO
       lvchange(8), vgs(8), vgdisplay(8), lvm(8)
